Third-party components in this model pack

plate_yolox_tiny_640.onnx
-------------------------
Produced by the open-lpr contributors. Architecture from YOLOX (Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX), under Apache-2.0. The model was pretrained on COCO and fine-tuned on an annotated license-plate corpus plus community-contributed images pseudo-labelled by a teacher model.

The publisher states that some community-contributed photos containing real plates, faces, and vehicles were uploaded without consent obtained. Those source images are not published or included here. Ultralytics YOLO weights are not used or redistributed.

plate_ocr_arabic_ppocrv3_mobile.onnx
plate_ocr_arabic_dict.json
-------------------------------------
The ONNX file is a format conversion of PaddleOCR's official `arabic_PP-OCRv3_mobile_rec` inference model, not a retrained model. Conversion provenance and immutable source revision are documented in `manifest.json`. PaddleOCR and its released model are Apache-2.0. The character dictionary is from the official PaddleOCR repository, with its Git blob pinned in the manifest.

The model and dictionary are a matched pair. The dictionary has 161 characters; CTC output class count is 163 (blank, dictionary characters, and space). The model can suggest Latin and Arabic/Persian letters and digits. PaddleOCR's reported 73.55% accuracy is for general Arabic text, not license plates. Persian digit forms and country-specific plate text accuracy are unvalidated. Every suggestion needs human review.
